      "message": "this is going to be confusing because the EC console logs are going\nto print \"C1\" but all the names are \"C2\". i assume this is also\ncalled C2 in the schematics?\n\nwe can handle non-consecutive port numbers by implementing\nboard_is_usb_pd_port_present(port) to check for only the valid\nport numbers. unfortunately, there are still numerous places\nin the code that explicitly check port numbers with\n(port \u003e\u003d 0) \u0026\u0026 (port \u003c board_get_usb_pd_port_count())\nwhich need to be updated.\n\nthe current EC code does support the case where\nboard_get_usb_pd_port_count() \u003c CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT\nbut it assumes the \"missing\" port is the highest numbered port.\n\nthere are some places that iterate over the ports from\n0..board_get_usb_pd_port_count() that probably should change\nto iterave over\n0..CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT and check \nboard_is_usb_pd_port_present() in the loop.",
